=== K. FINRA 2121: the official "5% Policy" is a guide, not a rule ===
2121: if a member buys for his own account from his customer, or sells for his own account to his customer,
  he shall buy or sell at a price which is fair, taking into consideration all relevant circumstances;
  and if he acts as agent for his customer, he shall not charge his customer more than a fair commission
  or service charge, taking into consideration all relevant circumstances
.01(1): The "5% Policy" is a guide, not a rule.
.01(4): A mark-up pattern of 5% or even less may be considered unfair or unreasonable under the "5% Policy."
It shall be deemed a violation of Rule 2010 and Rule 2121 for a member to enter into any transaction
  with a customer in any security at any price not reasonably related to the current market price of the security
  or to charge a commission which is not reasonable
.01(5): Determination of the fairness of mark-ups must be based on a consideration of all the relevant factors,
  of which the percentage of mark-up is only one
official Rule 2010 is cross-referenced; this toy is not a 2010 engine
